Raise the canonical scan matcher's CMake floor so that it configures under
CMake 4.

The matcher's build file asks for CMake 2.8 or newer. CMake 4.2.3, which this
image carries, refuses that outright: compatibility with anything below 3.5
has been removed, and the configure step stops before it reads another line.
Raising the floor to 3.10 is the whole of the fix. Nothing else in the build
file depends on the old behaviour, and afterwards the project configures with
no warning at all, not even the deprecation notice that a floor between 3.5
and 3.10 would still draw.

3.10 rather than 3.5 for that reason: 3.5 configures, but warns that it will
stop working, and a warning nobody can act on is worse than the smaller step
that removes it. Nothing in the build file uses a command newer than 3.10.

This is the Eigen variant of the matcher, on the `csm_eigen` branch, pinned at
commit 04c4a31072e8690bd0ff14de50be20c5b6b43e66. The other variant's build
file has a second fault of its own, a policy call CMake 4 no longer accepts.
This one does not: there is no policy call anywhere in it, and this single
line is the only build-file change needed.

Apply from the root of the matcher's own sources:

  patch -p1 < csm_cmake_floor.patch

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 ## This CMakeLists.txt file exists only for building as ROS 3rd-party package. Building for other purpose is not tested. See https://github.com/AndreaCensi/csm/pull/10
-cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 2.8)
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.10)
 project(csm)
 
 if(WIN32)
